  "judgements": [
    {
      "identity": "WAPT Community Edition 1.8.0.6641 Inno Setup installer",
      "verdict": "BENIGN",
      "evidence": [
        "Outer entry 0x41181c parses and checks Inno Setup 5.5.7 data, then reads installer records; extracted files form a consistent Python 2.7/WAPT application distribution.",
        "Authenticode image digest matches TRANQUIL IT SYSTEMS signature; certificate identifies the vendor and signed timestamp is 2020-01-23. Current trust-chain verification fails on expired/missing legacy roots; current validity is not asserted.",
        "WAPT CLI implements package install/remove/upgrade, host inventory, certificate pinning and signed-package management. These explain deployment/service/network/process APIs; no unauthorized deployment context was supplied.",
        "waptself.exe is the Lazarus self-service GUI: 143 RCDATA entries, 124 with PNG data, none with MZ/90/00. The largest (61152-byte TVISWAPTSELF) is a TPF0 form containing six PNG images. Resource APIs, process APIs and socket APIs are independent; their presence proves no resource-to-execution chain.",
        "setuphelpers_windows.py: get_all_scheduled_tasks line 256 creates Schedule.Service; critical_system_pending_updates line 2186 creates Microsoft.Update.Session. running_as_admin line 973 separately calls IsUserAnAdmin. This is not COM elevation.",
        "tclpip85.dll main 0x401000 parses a caller command line, handles standard streams via temporary files, invokes CreateProcessA at 0x4011aa, waits and relays output. Its small size is consistent with a Tcl pipe helper and does not establish staging.",
        "MFC90/MFC90U have consistent Visual Studio 2008 resource/PDB/export surfaces. Their unsigned Microsoft company claims plus URLMon references are not evidence of masquerading.",
        "jQuery UI draggable contains a real eval-based Packer wrapper. Offline radix-62/dictionary decoding yields 20539 bytes of drag/drop, selection, sortable and stacking UI code. The accurate suspicious Packer finding remains."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "Operator authorization and installation history are unknown. Administrative capabilities remain dual use; provenance alone is not the verdict."
      ]
    },
    {
      "identity": "label-core 0.1.12 queued files",
      "verdict": "BENIGN individually",
      "evidence": [
        "winshell.js and winshell.ts are corresponding source/transpiled PowerShell helpers. runScript wraps caller-supplied text, encodes UTF-16LE to Base64, launches PowerShell with EncodedCommand and ExecutionPolicy Bypass, collects stdout/stderr and returns status. Accurate execution/encoding/policy findings are retained.",
        "Callers query printers through Get-Printer/Get-CimInstance/Get-PrintJob or read clipboard text/images for labels. The exported functions are not install hooks or automatic remote payloads.",
        "config.ts reads/parses a caller-selected JSON file and writes/merges JSON. No hidden execution or network effect is present in this file.",
        "package.json describes the printer library, exports index.js, declares rendering dependencies, and has build/watch/release scripts without lifecycle install hooks. A files allowlist glob permits a hook filename but does not prove a hook is shipped."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "The archive conviction is retained by instruction; it is not inherited by these members. Other package/deployment evidence needed to explain that conviction was not supplied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "identity": "VidChain 0.8.3 and four fetched GitHub frontend assets",
      "archive_verdict": "MALICIOUS retained without re-judging",
      "member_verdict": "BENIGN individually",
      "evidence": [
        "Forager --all-wheels pkg:pypi/vidchain@0.8.3 retrieved one wheel with the original SHA256 a41a475be602cd26827feca38c51d3815b21dd6ba8e8528775d245a88b7ff440; it is an identical original, not a reconstruction.",
        "Reviewed Python paths implement user-supplied video processing, RAG/model calls, graph persistence, hardware monitoring and a FastAPI/dashboard server. The server binds 0.0.0.0 and serves local media; these are real exposures, not covert payload evidence. Pickle loading and chmod of an ffmpeg alias remain accurate capabilities.",
        "All four Forager-fetched assets hash-identically to their initial scan bytes. They are imported browser bundles from github.githubassets.com, reached through a core-js license page, not Python install-time payloads.",
        "code-view: source/image rendering, selection, copy controls, UI preference storage and cookie helpers. behaviors: delegated forms/search/navigation, clipboard success indicators and cross-tab login synchronization. react-core: routing, same-origin GitHub data requests and sessionStorage scroll restoration. 6n: Hotwired Turbo request/snapshot/navigation and configured WebSocket/EventSource streams, with CSRF-cookie-to-header handling.",
        "Their network, storage, cookie, DOM and clipboard observations describe ordinary website behavior and were preserved; no hostile or suspicious findings fired on these four files."
      ],
